    "notes": "Air-hardening tool steel (AISI A2 / DIN 1.2363). Properties listed for hardened and tempered condition (~200 °C temper, HRC 60). AZoM lists hardness as 64 HRC in the as-air-hardened condition (no temper); the database value of 60 HRC reflects the typical working condition after a 200 °C double-temper. Excellent dimensional stability during heat treatment due to balanced alloy content. Not recommended for welding in hardened state. Thermal conductivity (38 W/m·K) is higher than AZoM's figure; Online Metals value consistent with low Cr content (5%) vs. stainless steels (18% Cr, ~16 W/m·K)."
